# Shell scripts must check out LF everywhere: bash (incl. Git Bash on Windows) chokes on
# CRLF (`set -uo pipefail\r` is an invalid option), so an autocrlf checkout would install
# broken hooks and rails scripts — and broke the Windows CI leg running the hook tests.
# pwsh is CRLF-tolerant, so .ps1 files are left to the platform default.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Boards mirror's mini repositories are byte-exact test inputs: the `.proposed` writer's tests splice spans into
# them and compare against LF text, and the plan golden pins a hash over what they hold. An autocrlf checkout (Git for
# Windows' default) rewrote them CRLF, and the Windows leg alone failed. `eol=lf` wins over any core.autocrlf.
scripts/tests/fixtures/boards_repo*/** text eol=lf
